vations in service organizations: systematic review and recommendations</article-title><source>Milbank Q</source><year>2004</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>581</fpage><lpage>629</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15595944</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.0887-378X.2004.00325.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenhalgh</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Robert</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Macfarlane</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bate</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kyriakidou</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Peacock</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Storylines of research in diffusion of innovation: a meta-narrative approach to systematic review</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>417</fpage><lpage>430</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15893056</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2004.12.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Avant</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Strategies for theory construction in nursing</source><year>1995</year><edition>3</edition><publisher-name>Norwalk, CT: Appleton &#x00026; Lange</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Attwell</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rediscovering Apprenticeship? A Historical Approach</article-title><source>Paper presented at the European Conference on Educational Research</source><year>1997</year></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Simons</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Carden</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exploring Complementarity in On- and Off-Job Training for Apprenticeships</article-title><source>International Journal of Training and Development</source><year>2003</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>82</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/1468-2419.00173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Machles</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>A qualitative study of situated learning in occupational safety</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>North Carolina State University, Raleigh NC</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Considering Trade Union Education as a Community of Practice</article-title><source>International Journal of Lifelong Education</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>310</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/02601370304842</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Henning</surname><given-names>PH</given-names></name></person-group><source>A qualitative study of situated learning by refrigeration service technicians working for a supermarket chain in northeastern Pennsylvania</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>The Pennsylvania State University</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yi</su